    InApp SDK IntegrationStep 3: Start Pay Order

Step 3: Start Pay Order

In the steps of creating an order, the front-end App has already obtained the receive code receiveCode information from the front-end order creation interface. Next, the merchant app only needs to call the startPay API in the super app SDK, passing in the receiveCode, appId, and shortCode parameters to launch the Telebirr super app and enter the password to initiate the payment process. Below is an example of the API call.
3.1 Call the create order interface

The front-end page calls the back-end create order API to retrieve order information. rawRequest.
Create Order


    const title = "add your own title here"; // Replace with your desired title
    const amount = "add your own amount here"; // Replace with your desired amount

    function createOrder() {
     
        if (!amount) {
            return;
        }
        // call your backend create order api
        window.fetch(baseUrl + "/create/order", {
                method: "post",
                headers: {
                    "Content-Type": "application/json",
                },
                body: JSON.stringify({
                    title: title,
                    amount: amount,
                }),
            })
            .then((res) => {
                res.text()
                .then((receiveCode) => {
                    // call telebirr super app api to check out
                    this.startPay(receiveCode)
                })
                .catch((error) => {
                console.log("error occur", error);
                })
                .finally(() => {});
            });
        }

